From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
Subject: [PATCH] fcode: put xa+ and xa1+ into the 64-bit FCode table

The 64-bit FCode tokens of IEEE 1275's 64-bit extension run from 0x241
to 0x254. The table's 32-bit branch keeps that layout (seven reserved
tokens, /x at 0x248, twelve reserved tokens), but the 64-bit branch has
the entries for 0x24a and 0x24b commented out (and misnamed /xa+ and
/xa1+), so every token from 0x24a on runs the word two places further
down: xbflip runs at xa+'s token, ..., and xlsplit (0x251) runs xwflips.
forth/lib/64bit.fs defines xa+ and xa1+ already.

The illumos/Solaris ZFS boot block (zfs.fth, the "zfs-file-system"
package) uses xlsplit in its 64-bit compares (x0=, xcmp). Booting a
Tribblix (illumos) ZFS root disk on sun4u stopped right after the boot
block had loaded its file system package:

  Evaluating FCode...
  Unhandled Exception 0x0000000000000030
  PC = 0x00000000ffd0f498 NPC = 0x00000000ffd0f49c

(the PC in unaligned-l@: xwflips took the value to be split as an
address, 0). With the two entries in the table the boot block reads the
pool, loads the kernel and the boot archive from ZFS, and the system
boots.
---
 forth/device/table.fs | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/forth/device/table.fs b/forth/device/table.fs
index 04d22c8..9b00a6e 100644
--- a/forth/device/table.fs
+++ b/forth/device/table.fs
@@ -414,8 +414,8 @@ create fcode-master-table
   ['], x!
   ['], /x
   ['], /x*
-\   ['], /xa+
-\   ['], /xa1+
+  ['], xa+
+  ['], xa1+
   ['], xbflip
   ['], xbflips
   ['], xbsplit
